Title: RAIN ON MERIDIAN
Author: Walter Kane
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. MERIDIAN AVENUE - RAIN - NIGHT

Neon bleeds on wet asphalt. PRIVATE INVESTIGATOR FRANK MERCER, 45, turns up his collar. A CLIENT waits under a broken awning.
CLIENT
My husband keeps late hours at the Meridian Hotel. I want names.

INT. MERCER'S OFFICE - DAY

Frank develops photos — a woman in a RED HAT entering room 514. Not the client's husband. The husband follows, two hours later.
FRANK
Case wasn't infidelity. It was timing.

INT. MERIDIAN HOTEL - HALLWAY - NIGHT

Frank picks the lock on 514. Empty room — suitcase gone, bed still made. A matchbook on the nightstand: BLUE PARROT CLUB.

INT. BLUE PARROT CLUB - NIGHT

Smoke and jazz. The woman in the RED HAT sits with a man in a gray suit — the client's husband. They exchange a METAL CASE, not kisses.
FRANK
Ma'am, your husband isn't cheating. He's laundering.

INT. MERCER'S OFFICE - NIGHT

Rain hammers the window. The client returns — not worried wife, cold eyes. She slides an envelope across Frank's desk.
CLIENT
You were supposed to find a cheating husband. Not a partner.
FRANK
Then hire a worse detective next time.

FADE OUT.


THE END
